    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/yandex/odyssey/issues/995",
    "number": 995,
    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Fix segfault in large packets",
    "user": {
      "login": "GorComComputing",
      "id": 108394522,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBnX4Gg",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108394522?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/GorComComputing",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GorComComputing/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "The segfault occurs due to a signed integer overflow (it becomes negative).\r\nThe integer overflow happens when the size of a received PostgreSQL protocol packet exceeds 0x80000000 (2 GB).\r\n\r\nIn the PostgreSQL wire protocol, the packet size is specified as a 4-byte integer, which theoretically allows sending packets up to 4 GB in size.\r\nHowever, in practice, the Postgres server allocates memory blocks of up to 1 GB:\r\n```\r\n#define MaxAllocSize    ((Size) 0x3fffffff)\r\n```\r\nWhen receiving a packet, the server checks its length value, and if it exceeds 1 GB (0x3fffffff), it stops processing the packet and returns an error:\r\n```\r\ninvalid message length\r\n```\r\nTherefore, to fix the segfault, it was decided to add a handler that ensures the packet size does not exceed 0x80000000 (2 GB).\r\n",
